 "statement": "Annotated from the Beinecke scan alone (the right-hand panel of the '67r' canvas, with two crops). A wheel: an eight-pointed yellow star on a scalloped rosette at the centre with eight short words around it; a ring of twelve small moons, each a face inside a crescent, six red and six yellow, each with a short label; twelve wedge sectors holding short text, seven of them also holding a separate single word; twelve labels in red ink outside the sectors; and a rim band of tick-mark groups. Three lines of text run below the wheel, the middle one in red. Pairing used line ids and unit codes only: the twelve star-unit lines f67r2.52 to f67r2.63 to the moons and the twelve lines f67r2.1 to f67r2.12 to the sectors (as their red outer labels), both clockwise from twelve o'clock, which is an assumption about starting point and direction, so either ring may be rotated. The eight lines f67r2.64 to f67r2.71 are taken to be the words around the central star. The seven label lines that sit among the sector paragraphs (f67r2.15, 22, 28, 31, 34, 37, 47) are taken to be the single words inside sectors and are not tied to a drawn object.",
